From 0098ca8c5f69c1d2c8ff397a75d1915afc20872b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 16:49:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Collision: the actors of each cell in an open-addressed table

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Every trace, sweep and overlap test visits the 256-unit cells its box
covers and asks the collision system for each one's actors, most often
finding none. The cells were a std::unordered_map of std::lists: a lookup
took a 64-bit division for the bucket and a chain of dependent loads, and
on the handheld a third of TraceTester::Trace's own time was those
lookups. Every move of every actor also removed it from its cells and
added it again, a list node allocated and freed for each cell.

The cells are now an open-addressed table keyed by the same bucket id:
linear probing over a power-of-two array of ids, at most half full, so a
lookup is a multiply and, for an empty cell, usually one cache line. Each
cell's actors are an array in the order they were added, and removing an
actor keeps the others in order, as std::list::remove did, so every test
meets them in the same order as before. A cell keeps its slot once used;
an empty one iterates nothing, as an erased one did.

Checked with the frame time and random seeds temporarily fixed: a hash of
every actor's location, rotation, velocity, state and class matched the
build before patch 0028, frame by frame, on Liberty Island and UNATCO HQ,
and so did the logs.
